silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_05_sections_02_concrete_anchor_4#nodetypecorrection silm:hasLongDescription "The NodeTypeCorrection is the type tag for correction nodes pointing at pre-existing nodes. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Correction', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
